In the names and in the descriptions of the parameters, below there are often
aliases corresponding to the convention that 0 is the rational side and 1
is the algebraic side. If the two sides are algebraic, then the word
'rational' just means the side number 0. Note also that for a rational
side, the factor base is recomputed on the fly (or cached), and there is
no need to provide a fb0 parameter.

